  <entry>
    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2610.41104v1</id>
    <title>MUON-RT Reusing the Teacher's Trajectory for Momentum-Free Muon for LLM Self-Distillation</title>
    <updated>2026-10-30T00:50:49Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.41104v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2610.41104v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>Self-distillation methods for large language models with an exponential moving average (EMA) teacher already retain a history of student updates. Muon nevertheless stores a separate momentum buffer, increasing persistent training memory. We propose Muon with Reused Teacher (Muon-RT), which reuses the teacher-student displacement to eliminate momentum buffers for hidden weight matrices. We show that this displacement encodes an exponentially weighted history of applied updates and smooths temporally uncorrelated noise under a local model. Muon-RT removes its radial component, normalizes it spectrally, and mixes it with the current gradient after Newton-Schulz (NS) orthogonalization. Under explicit regularity and alignment assumptions, we establish linear contraction of an expected objective-gap bound toward a residual error level. With Self-Distillation Fine-Tuning (SDFT) on Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct, Muon-RT improves average accuracy over AdamW by 2.6 points with 42% less persistent memory, and over momentum Muon by 5.4 points with 27% less persistent memory. With Self-Distillation Policy Optimization (SDPO) on Olmo-3-7B-Instruct, it improves average accuracy over AdamW by 2.0 points.</summary>
    <category term="cs.LG" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <category term="cs.AI" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <category term="cs.CL" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <category term="stat.ML" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <published>2026-10-30T00:50:49Z</published>
    <arxiv:comment>Under Submission</arxiv:comment>
    <arxiv:primary_category term="cs.LG"/>
    <author>
      <name>Aryan Das</name>
    </author>
